  "final_message": "`service2.compute_fee(1000, \"gold\")` returns **480**. I worked it out by hand and got the same number by running the function.\n\n`service2` imports only `pricing` and `discounts`. Nothing imports `decoy_tax.py` or `decoy_shipping.py`, so they don't affect the result.\n\n1. `pricing.base_fee(1000)` returns 500 + 1000 // 10 = **600**.\n2. `discounts.apply_discount(600, \"gold\")` applies the 20% gold discount: 600 \u2212 (600 \u00d7 20) // 100 = 600 \u2212 120 = **480**.\n\nANSWER: 480",
